ant to what was missed. The 16.3% recall is the true partial-H1 recall; full H1 recall would be lower still. ROUND 1 HEURISTIC — the built-in heuristic (2.11×, σ=2.8 calcs) is better calibrated than H1. Its near-deterministic behavior and operation on the full pool implies it uses a richer feature set than a binary element + gap threshold. It does not discard hits. METHOD LIMITS — SLME values are MBJ-DFT upper bounds; defect tolerance, surface stability, and carrier mobility are unscored. Experimental validation (synthesis + J-V measurement) is required before any candidate is acted on. ONE REQUIRED FOLLOW-UP EXPERIMENT — compare_strategies(strategies=['random','surrogate'], seeds=10, leakage_guard=true, gap_min=0.5, gap_max=1.5) on the gap-only filtered pool (79 hits retained, 275 candidates, 28.7% base rate). This tests whether a gap-only pre-filter that passes the 60% recall gate can stack with BO to hit the ≥3.5× target and validates the gap range recalibration without the broken element assumption.",
